# Keycloak SSO for the Hubble UI is not part of the baseline; this file
# is the seam that work lands in. The baseline publishes the UI
# unauthenticated - route.yaml points the hubble listener at hubble-ui
# directly.
#
# What SSO adds:
#   - the `hubble` Keycloak client (inventory_keycloak_applications) and
#     its FreeIPA groups,
#   - an authenticating proxy in front of hubble-ui, following the
#     estate's longhorn-auth pattern (oauth2-proxy beside the service it
#     fronts, sealed client and cookie secrets),
#   - the HTTPRoute's backend switched from hubble-ui to that proxy.
#
# Until that lands, this file renders comment-only: the Kustomization
# resource list stays stable, so the SSO card replaces this file rather
# than rewiring the tree around it.
